---
import Alert from "@bundu/ui/app/Alert.astro";
import Badge from "@bundu/ui/app/Badge.astro";
import Card from "@bundu/ui/app/Card.astro";
import PageHeader from "@bundu/ui/app/PageHeader.astro";
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
import { CONSOLE_KEYS_URL, DOCS_URL, MAPS_API_BASE, MAPS_API_ENABLED } from "../config";
---
<Shell
  title="Docs"
  current="/docs/"
  description="The Nyuchi Maps contract: the OpenAPI document, the tile format and the credit rule."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Docs"
    description="What the service answers, how the tiles are shaped, and what you must show on every map."
    docsHref={DOCS_URL}
    docsLabel="Nyuchi docs"
  />

  <Card padding="md" class="grid gap-[14px]">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-[14px]">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-body font-semibold">The contract</h2>
        <p id="openapi-head" class="mt-1 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">Reading the OpenAPI document…</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/openapi.json" class="inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded-sm border border-border bg-card px-3.5 text-body-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring pointer-coarse:h-12">Open /openapi.json</a>
    </div>
    <p class="max-w-prose text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">This is the document this site serves, drawn here as it is. It describes the origin. {MAPS_API_ENABLED ? `The public API serves the same resources under ${MAPS_API_BASE}.` : `The public API will serve the same resources under ${MAPS_API_BASE} when the Maps API is enabled.`}</p>
    <div id="openapi" aria-busy="true" class="grid gap-[14px]"><p class="text-body-sm">Loading…</p></div>
  </Card>

  <Card padding="md" class="grid gap-[14px]">
    <h2 class="text-body font-semibold">The tile format</h2>
    <ul role="list" class="grid max-w-prose gap-[14px] text-body-sm">
      <li>Vector tiles in the Mapbox Vector Tile format, addressed as XYZ with the web-mercator grid. The TileJSON is version 3.0.0 and says the scheme is <code class="font-mono">xyz</code>.</li>
      <li>Tiles are served compressed and can be cached for a long time. The headers below are from a real tile, requested when this page opened.</li>
      <li>Styles, glyphs and sprites are served beside the tiles and never name a credit themselves: the TileJSON is the only place the credit comes from.</li>
    </ul>
    <dl id="tile-headers" class="grid gap-[14px] sm:grid-cols-[10rem_minmax(0,1fr)]"><dd class="text-body-sm">Requesting a sample tile…</dd></dl>
  </Card>

  <Card padding="md" class="grid gap-[14px]">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-[14px]">
      <h2 class="text-body font-semibold">Credits are mandatory</h2>
      <Badge variant="secondary">Licence condition</Badge>
    </div>
    <p class="max-w-prose text-body-sm">The base map is derived from open data under the Open Database Licence (ODbL), and the tiles are a Produced Work under it. The licence requires the credit wherever the map is shown. This is a condition of using the tiles, not a courtesy.</p>
    <ol class="grid max-w-prose list-decimal gap-[14px] pl-5 text-body-sm">
      <li>Show the credit on every map you draw from these tiles, always visible or one tap away behind a small (i).</li>
      <li>Take the text and its link from the TileJSON's <code class="font-mono">attribution</code> field. Do not retype it: the field is the one source, and it can change.</li>
      <li>MapLibre GL JS, the Leaflet adapter and OpenLayers read the credit from the TileJSON and show it for you. Keep their attribution control switched on.</li>
      <li>If you draw tiles yourself, or export an image, put the credit in the picture.</li>
      <li>There is no setting to hide the credit on an embed, and there will not be one.</li>
    </ol>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-body-sm font-semibold">The credit the service returns right now</h3>
      <ul id="credit-live" role="list" class="mt-2 grid gap-[14px] text-body-sm"><li>Loading…</li></ul>
    </div>
  </Card>

  <Alert variant="info" title="Keys and the public API">
    <p>The public Maps API is the Nyuchi API at <span class="font-mono">{MAPS_API_BASE}</span>{MAPS_API_ENABLED ? "." : ", available when the Maps API is enabled."} Keys are created and managed in the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href={CONSOLE_KEYS_URL}>Nyuchi Console</a>, not on this site.</p>
  </Alert>
</Shell>

<script>
  import "../scripts/docs.js";
</script>
